  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP Integrated food security project in Akobo (East &amp; West) County, South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is funded by World Food Programme(WFP) and will assist 81,935 vulnerable women and girls, returnees and internally displaced persons affected by crises in Akobo Counties of Jonglei State in South Sudan with General Food Distribution (GFD) and Blanket Supplementary Feeding (BSF) through provision of nutrition -sensitive food assistance (In -Kind).  Beneficiaries (32,786) will also be engaged in Asset Creation and Livelihoods (ACL) activities, and they will receive either cash or in -kind support.  The project also has a School Feeding (SF) component aimed at improving enrolment, attendance, and gender disparities of 8500 boys and girls in 14 targeted schools in Akobo counties by December 2024 through provision of daily hot school meals. 2502 beneficiaries will be supported with Smallholder Agriculture &amp; Market Support interventions. The project runs from 1 January 2024 to 31 December 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
